cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "FM-REG-01: Mirror-symmetry decomposition of the crack-tip J-integral"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
authors:
  - family-names: Politzer
    given-names: Brian Scott
repository-code: "https://github.com/gringomxmusic-byte/FM-REG-01"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - fracture mechanics
  - J-integral
  - mixed-mode fracture
  - mirror symmetry
  - Williams expansion
abstract: >-
  Numerical verification that the mirror operator (Ma)(x) = R a(Rx), with
  R = diag(1,-1,1) reflecting across the crack plane, splits the J-integral of
  exact Williams near-tip fields into a mirror-even part K_I^2/E' and a
  mirror-odd part K_II^2/E' + K_III^2/(2 mu), with zero cross-coupling and
  path independence (21/21 checks).
